ite22†Image: github cite23†Image: huggingface cite24†Image: x --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew Released - Overview - Z.AI DEVELOPER DOCUMENT (https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released)\nciteturn2560view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: > ## Documentation Index\nL1: >\nL2: > Fetch the complete documentation index at: cite0†/llms.txt L3: >\nL4: > Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Skip to main content L7: \nL8: cite2†Overview - Z.AI DEVELOPER DOCUMENT home page†z.ai L9: \nL10: Search...\nL11: \nL12: Navigation\nL13: \nL14: New Released\nL15: \nL16: cite3†Guides cite4†API Reference cite5†Coding Plan cite6†Released Notes cite7†Terms and Policy cite8†Help Center L17: \nL18: # New Released\nL19: \nL20: Follow along with updates across Z.AI’s models\nL21: \nL22: Copy page Copy page\nL23: ##\nL24: \nL25: cite9†​ L26: \nL27: Models\nL28: \nL29: cite10†​ L30: \nL31: [Button: 2026-08-26]\nL32: \nL33: GLM-5.3-Flash\nL34:   * Native visual capabilities enable the model to observe interfaces, rendering results, and interaction feedback—creating a closed loop across code, browsers, and GUIs.\nL35:   * Efficient hybrid architecture: Combines linear and sparse attention with 320B total parameters and 18B activated, significantly reducing compute and KV-cache requirements.\nL36:   * Beyond coding: Supports office document and financial research workflows, autonomously breaking down goals, using tools, and refining outputs. Learn more in our cite11†documentation .*\nL37: cite12†​ L38: \nL39: [Button: 2026-08-18]\nL40: \nL41: GLM-5.3\nL42:   * Stronger Coding Capabilities: GLM-5.3 delivers a significant improvement in coding capabilities, achieving a 50% gain over GLM-5.2 on Z.ai Code Bench and reaching state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance among open-source models on public benchmarks, including Terminal Bench 3.0.\nL43:   * Emergent Cybersecurity Capabilities: GLM-5.3 matches Mythos 5 in white-box code review and vulnerability discovery. In collaboration with multiple cybersecurity teams, it has been tested on real-world targets and has identified a total of 2,436 vulnerabilities, including 1,097 medium- and high-severity vulnerabilities.Learn more in our cite13†documentation .*\nL44: cite14†​ L45: \nL46: [Button: 2026-06-16]\nL47: \nL48: GLM-5.2\nL49:   * Supports 1M lossless context, significantly improving long-horizon task capabilities and reducing context drift and goal forgetting in complex tasks\nL50:   * Achieves open-source SOTA performance on coding and long-horizon task benchmarks, delivering more stable results in complex system engineering and deep debugging\nL51:   * Significantly improves the real-world developer experience, with more reliable project-level context handling, adherence to engineering standards, and multi-platform development. Learn more in our cite15†documentation .*\nL52: cite16†​ L53: \nL54: [Button: 2026-04-07]\nL55: \nL56: GLM-5.1\nL57:   * Designed for long-horizon tasks, GLM-5.1 can work independently for up to 8 hours in a single run, enabling a full loop from planning and execution to iterative refinement and final delivery.\nL58:   * It demonstrates stronger engineering intelligence across autonomous planning, sustained execution, bug fixing, and strategy iteration, while achieving comprehensive capability alignment with Claude Opus 4.6. Built with multi-turn SFT, RL, and a process-quality evaluation framework, GLM-5.1 further improves stability, consistency, and tool use over extended tasks. Learn more in our cite17†documentation .*\nL59: cite18†​ L60: \nL61: [Button: 2026-02-12]\nL62: \nL63: GLM-5\nL64:   * Designed for complex system engineering and long-range Agent tasks, GLM-5 shifts the paradigm from coding to engineering, demonstrating strong deep-reasoning performance in backend architecture, complex algorithms, and stubborn bug fixing.\nL65:   * It directly benchmarks against Claude Opus 4.5 in code-logic density and systems-engineering capability, and integrates DeepSeek Sparse Attention for higher token efficiency while preserving long-context quality.Learn more in our cite19†documentation .*\nL66: \nL67: cite20†​ L68: [Button: 2026-02-03]\nL69: \nL70: GLM-OCR\nL71:   * We’ve launched GLM-OCR, a compact and high-performance optical character recognition model powered by the self-developed CogViT and GLM-0.5B encoder-decoder architecture, enabling efficient cross-modal alignment through its dedicated connection layer.\nL72:   * The update leverages CLIP pre-training on billions of image-text pairs to deliver robust visual semantic understanding and key token extraction capabilities, while maintaining a lightweight design for fast inference. Learn more in our cite21†documentation .*\nL73: cite22†​ L74: \nL75: [Button: 2026-01-19]\nL76: \nL77: GLM-4.7-Flash\nL78:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.7-Flash, a lightweight and efficient model designed as the free-tier version of GLM-4.7, delivering strong performance across coding, reasoning, and generative tasks with low latency and high throughput.\nL79:   * The update brings competitive coding capabilities at its scale, offering best-in-class general abilities in writing, translation, long-form content, role play, and aesthetic outputs for high-frequency and real-time use cases. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\nL80: \nL81: cite24†​ L82: [Button: 2026-01-14]\nL83: \nL84: GLM-Image\nL85:   * We’ve launched GLM-Image, a state-of-the-art image generation model built on a multimodal architecture and fully trained on domestic chips, combining autoregressive semantic understanding with diffusion-based decoding to deliver high-quality, controllable visual generation.\nL86:   * The update significantly enhances performance in knowledge-intensive scenarios, with more stable and accurate text rendering inside images, making GLM-Image especially well suited for commercial design, educational illustrations, and content-rich visual applications.Learn more in our cite25†documentation .*\nL87: cite26†​ L88: \nL89: [Button: 2025-12-22]\nL90: \nL91: GLM-4.7\nL92:   * We’ve released GLM-4.7, our foundation model with significant improvements in coding, reasoning, and agentic capabilities. It delivers more reliable code generation, stronger long-context understanding, and improved end-to-end task execution across real-world development workflows.\nL93:   * The update brings open-source SOTA performance on major coding and reasoning benchmarks, enhanced agentic coding for goal-driven, multi-step tasks, and improved front-end and document generation quality. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\nL94: cite27†​ L95: \nL96: [Button: 2025-12-11]\nL97: \nL98: AutoGLM-Phone-Multilingual\nL99:   * We’ve launched AutoGLM-Phone-Multilingual, our latest multimodal mobile automation framework that understands screen content and executes real actions through ADB. It enables natural-language task execution across 50+ mainstream apps, delivering true end-to-end mobile control.\nL100:   * The update introduces multilingual support (English & Chinese), enhanced workflow planning capabilities, and improved task execution reliability. Learn more in our cite28†documentation .*\nL101: \nL102: cite29†​ L103: \nL104: [Button: 2025-12-10]\nL105: GLM-ASR-2512\nL106: \nL107:   * We’ve launched GLM-ASR-2512, our ASR model, delivering industry-leading accuracy with a Character Error Rate of just 0.0717, and significantly improved performance across real-world multilingual and accent-rich scenarios.\nL108:   * The update introduces enhanced custom dictionary support and expanded specialized terminology recognition. Learn more in our cite30†documentation .*\nL109: \nL110: cite31†​ L111: \nL112: [Button: 2025-12-08]\nL113: \nL114: GLM-4.6V\nL115:   * We’re excited to introduce GLM-4.6V, Z.ai’s latest iteration in multimodal large language models. This version enhances vision understanding, achieving state-of-the-art performance in tasks involving images and text.\nL116:   * The update also expands the context window to 128K, enabling more efficient processing of long inputs and complex multimodal tasks. Learn more in our cite32†documentation .*\nL117: \nL118: cite33†​ L119: \nL120: [Button: 2025-09-30]\nL121: \nL122: GLM-4.6\n"
